   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the name of the\nRockland County Solid Waste Authority, subjecting such authority to regulation\nby the department of agriculture and markets, and making a technical change;\nand to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to public\nauthorities providing shelter services for the care of unwanted animals",
    "basePrintNo": "S9530",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9530-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§2053-b, 2053-c, 2053-e & 2053-g, Pub Auth L; amd §§114 & 400, Ag & Mkts L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9530\n\nSPONSOR: WEBER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the name of\nthe Rockland County Solid Waste Authority, subjecting such authority to\nregulation by the department of agriculture and markets, and making a\ntechnical change; and to amend the agriculture and markets law, in\nrelation to public authorities providing shelter services for the care\nof unwanted animals\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would permit Rockland Green and/or RG Cares to operate an\nanimal shelter within Rockland County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n  Section  1:  Amends section 2053-b of the public authorities law as it\nrelates to definitions.\n\n  Section 2: Amends section 2053-c of the public authorities law  as  it\nrelates to the title of the authority.\n\n  Section  3:  Amends section 2053-e of the public authorities law as it\nrelates to the responsibilities of the authority.\n\n  Section 4: Amends section 20531 of the public authorities  law  as  it\nrelates to charges of the authority.\n\n  Section 5: Amends section 114 of the agriculture and markets law as it\nrelates  to  clarifying  entities  authorized  to  contract with munici-\npalities for shelter services.\n\n  Section 6: Amends section 400 of the agriculture and markets law as it\nrelates to pet dealers.\n\n  Section 7: Amends section 114 of the agriculture and markets law as it\nrelates to exemptions from the pet dealer definition.\n\n  Section 8: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is introduced to clarify legislation passed in 2022 related to\nthe operation of animal shelter services in Rockland County.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately provided that  section  seven  of\nthis  act  shall  take effect on the same date and in the same manner as\nchapter 681 of the laws of 2022 takes effect.\n",
